---
import PlaygroundShell from '../components/PlaygroundShell.astro';
---
<PlaygroundShell title="Simulate it" hint="Prefix search over generated keys, three ways, counted in character steps (one step is a character compared or a trie node entered), never timed. The memory side counts trie nodes and child slots, not bytes.">
  <ol class="how">
    <li>Start with <b>Keys</b> "Word-like", <b>Number of keys</b> <b>10,000</b>, <b>Prefix length</b> <b>4</b> (the prefix "taka") and <b>Return</b> "All matches": scanning every key costs <b>11,945</b> steps, binary search over the sorted keys <b>238</b>, the trie <b>102</b>, and all three find <b>48</b> matches.</li>
    <li>Set <b>Return</b> to "First 10 matches", as an autocomplete box would: the scan still costs <b>3,262</b> steps, the trie only <b>21</b>.</li>
    <li>Set <b>Prefix length</b> to <b>1</b> and <b>Return</b> back to "All matches": the answer is huge, <b>1,245</b> keys. Now the sorted array wins with <b>1,259</b> steps against <b>2,592</b> for the trie, because the trie has to visit every inner node under "t".</li>
    <li>Set <b>Keys</b> to "Random ids": 10,000 keys of 8 letters have <b>80,000</b> characters but a trie of <b>58,243</b> nodes, which is <b>1,514,318</b> child slots if every node holds 26 slots. A compressed (radix) tree needs only <b>12,704</b> nodes.</li>
  </ol>
  <div class="pg tr" data-tr>
    <div class="pg-row">
      <label>Keys <select class="pg-in" data-kind><option value="words" selected>Word-like</option><option value="ids">Random ids</option></select></label>
      <label>Number of keys <select class="pg-in" data-n><option value="100">100</option><option value="1000">1,000</option><option value="10000" selected>10,000</option></select></label>
      <label>Prefix length <select class="pg-in" data-len><option value="1">1</option><option value="2">2</option><option value="3">3</option><option value="4" selected>4</option></select></label>
      <label>Return <select class="pg-in" data-limit><option value="0" selected>All matches</option><option value="10">First 10 matches</option></select></label>
    </div>
    <div class="pg-grid">
      <div class="pg-box" data-b1><h3>Scan every key</h3><span class="pg-mono tr-big" data-o1></span><span class="pg-note">steps; what a hash map or plain list must do</span></div>
      <div class="pg-box" data-b2><h3>Sorted keys, binary search</h3><span class="pg-mono tr-big" data-o2></span><span class="pg-note">steps</span></div>
      <div class="pg-box" data-b3><h3>Trie</h3><span class="pg-mono tr-big" data-o3></span><span class="pg-note">steps</span></div>
      <div class="pg-box" style="--c: var(--role-1)"><h3>Matches found</h3><span class="pg-mono tr-big" data-found></span><span class="pg-note" data-prefix></span></div>
    </div>
    <div class="pg-box" style="--c: var(--border)">
      <h3>Steps, log scale</h3>
      <div class="tr-bars" data-bars></div>
    </div>
    <div class="pg-grid">
      <div class="pg-box" style="--c: var(--role-1)"><h3>Characters stored</h3><span class="pg-mono tr-big" data-chars></span><span class="pg-note">in the keys themselves</span></div>
      <div class="pg-box" data-m2><h3>Trie nodes</h3><span class="pg-mono tr-big" data-nodes></span><span class="pg-note" data-nodesn></span></div>
      <div class="pg-box" data-m3><h3>Child slots, 26 per node</h3><span class="pg-mono tr-big" data-slots></span><span class="pg-note">if each node holds an array for a to z</span></div>
      <div class="pg-box" style="--c: var(--good)"><h3>Radix tree nodes</h3><span class="pg-mono tr-big" data-radix></span><span class="pg-note">only the root, word ends and branch points</span></div>
    </div>
    <p class="pg-out" data-verdict role="status"></p>
    <p class="pg-note">Assumptions: keys are lowercase letters; "Word-like" keys are 2 to 4 syllables from a list of 16, so prefixes repeat; "Random ids" are 8 random letters. Trie children are visited in letter order. Binary search counts characters compared, like the scan. A real trie spends more per node than one character (pointers, flags), which is why node counts matter more than character counts. Fixed generator, so results repeat.</p>
  </div>
</PlaygroundShell>
<script>
  import { query, formatThousands } from '../playground';
  const SYLLABLES = ['ka', 'ro', 'mi', 'te', 'su', 'no', 'la', 'pe', 'vi', 'do', 'an', 'el', 'or', 'in', 'ta', 'ge'];
  const ALPHABET = 26;
  const TYPED = 'taka';
  interface TNode { kids: Map<string, number>; end: boolean }

  // The same model as the code samples, ported to TypeScript.
  function makeWords(kind: string, n: number): string[] {
    let x = 12345;
    const next = () => { x = (Math.imul(x, 1664525) + 1013904223) >>> 0; return x >>> 16; };
    const seen = new Set<string>();
    const words: string[] = [];
    while (words.length < n) {
      let w = '';
      if (kind === 'words') { const parts = 2 + (next() % 3); for (let i = 0; i < parts; i++) w += SYLLABLES[next() % 16]; }
      else for (let i = 0; i < 8; i++) w += String.fromCharCode(97 + (next() % 26));
      if (!seen.has(w)) { seen.add(w); words.push(w); }
    }
    return words;
  }
  function scanSearch(words: string[], prefix: string, limit: number) {
    let steps = 0, found = 0;
    for (const w of words) {
      let i = 0;
      while (i < prefix.length) { steps++; if (i >= w.length || w[i] !== prefix[i]) break; i++; }
      if (i === prefix.length) { found++; if (limit > 0 && found === limit) break; }
    }
    return { steps, found };
  }
  function sortedSearch(sorted: string[], prefix: string, limit: number) {
    let steps = 0;
    const cmp = (w: string) => {
      for (let i = 0; i < prefix.length; i++) { steps++; if (i >= w.length) return -1; if (w[i] !== prefix[i]) return w[i] < prefix[i] ? -1 : 1; }
      return 0;
    };
    let lo = 0, hi = sorted.length;
    while (lo < hi) { const mid = (lo + hi) >> 1; if (cmp(sorted[mid]) < 0) lo = mid + 1; else hi = mid; }
    let found = 0;
    for (let i = lo; i < sorted.length && cmp(sorted[i]) === 0; i++) { found++; if (limit > 0 && found === limit) break; }
    return { steps, found };
  }
  function buildTrie(words: string[]): TNode[] {
    const nodes: TNode[] = [{ kids: new Map(), end: false }];
    for (const w of words) {
      let at = 0;
      for (const c of w) {
        if (!nodes[at].kids.has(c)) { nodes.push({ kids: new Map(), end: false }); nodes[at].kids.set(c, nodes.length - 1); }
        at = nodes[at].kids.get(c)!;
      }
      nodes[at].end = true;
    }
    return nodes;
  }
  function trieSearch(nodes: TNode[], prefix: string, limit: number) {
    let steps = 0, found = 0, at = 0;
    for (const c of prefix) { if (!nodes[at].kids.has(c)) return { steps: steps + 1, found: 0 }; steps++; at = nodes[at].kids.get(c)!; }
    const visit = (id: number): boolean => {
      if (nodes[id].end) found++;
      if (limit > 0 && found >= limit) return true;
      for (const c of [...nodes[id].kids.keys()].sort()) { steps++; if (visit(nodes[id].kids.get(c)!)) return true; }
      return false;
    };
    visit(at);
    return { steps, found };
  }
  const compressedNodes = (nodes: TNode[]) => nodes.filter((nd, i) => i === 0 || nd.end || nd.kids.size >= 2).length;

  const cache = new Map<string, { words: string[]; sorted: string[]; nodes: TNode[]; chars: number; radix: number }>();
  function dataset(kind: string, n: number) {
    const key = `${kind}:${n}`;
    if (!cache.has(key)) {
      const words = makeWords(kind, n);
      const nodes = buildTrie(words);
      cache.set(key, { words, sorted: [...words].sort(), nodes, chars: words.reduce((s, w) => s + w.length, 0), radix: compressedNodes(nodes) });
    }
    return cache.get(key)!;
  }

  document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-tr]').forEach((root) => {
    const q = query(root);
    const val = (s: string) => q<HTMLSelectElement>(s).value;
    const colour = (s: string, c: string) => q<HTMLElement>(s).style.setProperty('--c', c);
    function draw() {
      const kind = val('[data-kind]'), n = Number(val('[data-n]')), len = Number(val('[data-len]')), limit = Number(val('[data-limit]'));
      const d = dataset(kind, n);
      const p = TYPED.slice(0, len);
      const a = scanSearch(d.words, p, limit), b = sortedSearch(d.sorted, p, limit), c = trieSearch(d.nodes, p, limit);
      q('[data-o1]').textContent = formatThousands(a.steps);
      q('[data-o2]').textContent = formatThousands(b.steps);
      q('[data-o3]').textContent = formatThousands(c.steps);
      const best = Math.min(a.steps, b.steps, c.steps);
      colour('[data-b1]', a.steps === best ? 'var(--good)' : 'var(--bad)');
      colour('[data-b2]', b.steps === best ? 'var(--good)' : 'var(--role-1)');
      colour('[data-b3]', c.steps === best ? 'var(--good)' : 'var(--role-1)');
      q('[data-found]').textContent = formatThousands(c.found);
      q('[data-prefix]').textContent = `prefix "${p}"${limit > 0 ? `, stopping after ${limit}` : ''}`;
      const bars = q('[data-bars]');
      bars.textContent = '';
      const top = Math.log10(Math.max(10, a.steps, b.steps, c.steps));
      for (const [name, v] of [['Scan', a.steps], ['Sorted + binary search', b.steps], ['Trie', c.steps]] as [string, number][]) {
        const row = document.createElement('div'); row.className = 'tr-bar';
        const label = document.createElement('span'); label.textContent = name;
        const track = document.createElement('span'); track.className = 'tr-track';
        const fill = document.createElement('span'); fill.className = 'tr-fill'; fill.style.width = `${Math.max(2, (Math.log10(Math.max(1, v)) / top) * 100)}%`;
        track.appendChild(fill);
        const num = document.createElement('span'); num.className = 'pg-mono'; num.textContent = formatThousands(v);
        row.append(label, track, num); bars.appendChild(row);
      }
      q('[data-chars]').textContent = formatThousands(d.chars);
      q('[data-nodes]').textContent = formatThousands(d.nodes.length);
      q('[data-nodesn]').textContent = `${formatThousands(d.nodes.length)} nodes for ${formatThousands(d.chars)} characters`;
      colour('[data-m2]', d.nodes.length > d.chars / 2 ? 'var(--bad)' : 'var(--role-1)');
      q('[data-slots]').textContent = formatThousands(d.nodes.length * ALPHABET);
      colour('[data-m3]', d.nodes.length * ALPHABET > 10 * d.chars ? 'var(--bad)' : 'var(--role-1)');
      q('[data-radix]').textContent = formatThousands(d.radix);
      const slotRatio = Math.round((d.nodes.length * ALPHABET) / d.chars);
      q('[data-verdict]').textContent = c.steps < b.steps
        ? `The trie answers in ${formatThousands(c.steps)} steps whatever the number of keys: its cost follows the prefix length and the answer size. Its price is memory: ${formatThousands(d.nodes.length)} nodes, and ${slotRatio} child slots per stored character if each node is a 26-slot array.`
        : `Here the sorted array wins: with ${formatThousands(c.found)} matches the trie has to visit every inner node under the prefix, while the sorted array reads matching keys one after another. A trie is not automatically the cheapest.`;
    }
    root.addEventListener('change', draw);
    draw();
  });
</script>
<style is:global>
  .playground .tr-big { font-size: 1.15rem; font-weight: 600; }
  .playground .tr-bars { display: grid; gap: 6px; }
  .playground .tr-bar { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 9.5rem 1fr; gap: 2px 8px; align-items: center; }
  .playground .tr-bar .pg-mono { grid-column: 2; }
  .playground .tr-track { display: block; height: 12px; border-radius: 6px; background: var(--surface-2); overflow: hidden; }
  .playground .tr-fill { display: block; height: 100%; background: var(--accent); border-radius: 6px; }
  @media (max-width: 520px) { .playground .tr-bar { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } .playground .tr-bar .pg-mono { grid-column: 1; } }
</style>
